{
  "_id": "SolCombatTrain01",
  "name": "Combat Training",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/skills/combat/hand-to-hand-fighting-stance.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<h3>Fighting Style</h3>\n<p>You have honed your martial prowess and gain one Fighting Style of your choice. Whenever you gain a Soldier level, you can replace the chosen Fighting Style with another one of your choice.</p>\n<h3>Weapon Mastery</h3>\n<p>Your training with weapons allows you to use the mastery properties of three kinds of weapons of your choice with which you have proficiency. Whenever you finish a <strong>Long Rest</strong>, you can change the kinds of weapons you have chosen.</p>\n<h3>Second Wind</h3>\n<p>You have a limited well of stamina that you can draw on to protect yourself from harm. On your turn, you can use a <strong>Bonus Action</strong> to regain hit points equal to <strong>1d10 + your Soldier level</strong>.</p>\n<p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your <strong>Proficiency Bonus</strong> (`@prof`). You regain one expended use when you finish a <strong>Short Rest</strong>, and all expended uses when you finish a <strong>Long Rest</strong>. You can also expend 2 Nanopool points to regain one expended use of Second Wind.</p>\n<h3>Tactical Mind</h3>\n<p>When you fail an ability check, you can expend one use of your <strong>Second Wind</strong> (or spend 2 Nanopool points) to push yourself toward success. Rather than rolling the die and regaining hit points, you roll <strong>1d10</strong> and add the number rolled to the ability check, potentially turning the failure into a success. If the check still fails, this use of Second Wind is not expended.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
